  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115864",
      "title": "Analyzing a Built-in Attribute Directive: ngModel",
      "lectureOrder": 153,
      "videoOrder": 145,
      "sourceHash": "7547a368cd31845418e432c2a3dad58c5abf00aba09a1c739b3da97c77591852",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.54,
          "end": 3.45,
          "en": "So inside this starting project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.45,
          "end": 5.19,
          "en": "which I provided to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.19,
          "end": 9.54,
          "en": "if you take a look at the auth.component template file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.54,
          "end": 13.65,
          "en": "you'll see that, in there, directive gets used,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.65,
          "end": 17.362,
          "en": "a built-in directive, the ngModel directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.362,
          "end": 20.19,
          "en": "which we have used before in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.19,
          "end": 24.81,
          "en": "to set up two-way binding, which allows us to get the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.81,
          "end": 27.33,
          "en": "the user entered upon every keystroke",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.33,
          "end": 30.6,
          "en": "and save it into a value of our choice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.6,
          "end": 32.73,
          "en": "in this case, into an email property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.73,
          "end": 34.53,
          "en": "which, here, is a signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.53,
          "end": 37.05,
          "en": "which, as you learned before, doesn't matter though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.05,
          "end": 38.733,
          "en": "It doesn't have to be a signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.29,
          "end": 43.41,
          "en": "and then we could, also, set a new value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.41,
          "end": 46.71,
          "en": "for email or password, and that would be sent back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.71,
          "end": 50.55,
          "en": "into the input elements, again, with two-way binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.55,
          "end": 53.82,
          "en": "but two-way binding, as you also learned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.82,
          "end": 58.82,
          "en": "is not a feature that only exists for this ngModel thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.46,
          "end": 61.41,
          "en": "instead, as you saw before in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.41,
          "end": 63.12,
          "en": "you can set up two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.12,
          "end": 65.94,
          "en": "for your own components as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.94,
          "end": 68.28,
          "en": "instead, ngModel is simply a directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.28,
          "end": 73.05,
          "en": "that enhances input elements, including text areas",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.05,
          "end": 77.58,
          "en": "or select dropdown elements such that they do support",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.58,
          "end": 80.88,
          "en": "two-way binding through that directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.88,
          "end": 83.52,
          "en": "So it enhances those elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.52,
          "end": 87.18,
          "en": "but it does not bring its own template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.18,
          "end": 90.99,
          "en": "When we add ngModel on an input here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.99,
          "end": 94.02000000000001,
          "en": "you'll see that if you inspect that input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.02000000000001,
          "end": 96.87,
          "en": "the content of that element didn't change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.87,
          "end": 100.32300000000001,
          "en": "There was no template content rendered into it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.58,
          "end": 104.52000000000001,
          "en": "What you can see though, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.52000000000001,
          "end": 107.7,
          "en": "is that there also are some CSS classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.7,
          "end": 110.1,
          "en": "being added to that input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.1,
          "end": 112.89,
          "en": "Some classes which start with ng-,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.89,
          "end": 115.08,
          "en": "which is always a good indicator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.08,
          "end": 118.38,
          "en": "if something starts with ng, that it's coming",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.38,
          "end": 122.37,
          "en": "from the Angular framework itself and not from us,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.37,
          "end": 126.3,
          "en": "and, indeed, I don't have those classes on the input here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.3,
          "end": 131.3,
          "en": "So ngModel, besides allowing us to perform two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.21,
          "end": 135.873,
          "en": "also seems to be responsible for adding these classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.01,
          "end": 139.65,
          "en": "Now, we'll take a closer look at these classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.65,
          "end": 142.26,
          "en": "and why they're added and what they're doing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.26,
          "end": 145.65,
          "en": "later in this course in the forms course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.65,
          "end": 148.17000000000002,
          "en": "because, in the end, these classes are added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.17000000000002,
          "end": 151.29,
          "en": "and updated dynamically by ngModel",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.29,
          "end": 153.3,
          "en": "on input elements like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.3,
          "end": 156.69,
          "en": "to reflect whether a valid value has been added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.69,
          "end": 160.8,
          "en": "whether the user has interacted with an input, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 160.8,
          "end": 163.5,
          "en": "For example, if I inspect that password input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 163.5,
          "end": 165.36,
          "en": "before clicking into it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.36,
          "end": 169.2,
          "en": "you see that it has the ng-untouched class on it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 169.2,
          "end": 172.38,
          "en": "and if I do click into it, and then go out of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 172.38,
          "end": 175.86,
          "en": "you see that that changed, and, now, it's ng-touched.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 175.86,
          "end": 179.07,
          "en": "So that's also something ngModel is doing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 179.07,
          "end": 182.73,
          "en": "besides allowing us to perform two-way binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 182.73,
          "end": 185.79,
          "en": "because, as I mentioned before on this slide,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.79,
          "end": 189.42,
          "en": "you could also use ngModel without two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 189.42,
          "end": 192.51,
          "en": "if you don't need that feature to, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 192.51,
          "end": 196.53,
          "en": "still get these dynamically managed CSS classes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 196.53,
          "end": 200.28,
          "en": "which you could use for dynamically styling these inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.28,
          "end": 203.01,
          "en": "depending on whether they hold valid values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 203.01,
          "end": 205.59,
          "en": "and the user has interacted with them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 205.59,
          "end": 208.2,
          "en": "but, again, that is something we'll take a closer look at",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 208.2,
          "end": 210.21,
          "en": "later in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 210.21,
          "end": 213.57,
          "en": "For now, it's just important to understand that ngModel",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 213.57,
          "end": 216.75,
          "en": "is such a directive offered by Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 216.75,
          "end": 218.7,
          "en": "as you can also tell by the name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 218.7,
          "end": 221.82,
          "en": "which enhances input elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 221.82,
          "end": 224.43,
          "en": "by allowing us to perform two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 224.43,
          "end": 227.97,
          "en": "or by managing those CSS classes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 227.97,
          "end": 231.45,
          "en": "and, indeed, if you take a look at the source code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 231.45,
          "end": 233.7,
          "en": "of Angular, which you can access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 233.7,
          "end": 236.22,
          "en": "since it's an open source project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 236.22,
          "end": 240.36,
          "en": "you'll see that this ngModel directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 240.36,
          "end": 244.08,
          "en": "does indeed do a lot of things internally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 244.08,
          "end": 246.21,
          "en": "Now, you don't need to understand all that code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 246.21,
          "end": 248.01,
          "en": "It is rather complex, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 248.01,
          "end": 250.59,
          "en": "because it is a rather complex directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 250.59,
          "end": 253.68,
          "en": "but one thing you can, for example, see in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 253.68,
          "end": 258.45,
          "en": "is that it has an input, which is internally named model,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 258.45,
          "end": 261.57,
          "en": "but which then has an alias of ngModel,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 261.57,
          "end": 265.803,
          "en": "and that it has an output named ngModelChange,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 266.94,
          "end": 269.04,
          "en": "and that, for example, is why we can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 269.04,
          "end": 273.21,
          "en": "two-way binding on that ngModel directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 273.21,
          "end": 275.19,
          "en": "because it has these properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 275.19,
          "end": 278.433,
          "en": "which follow this two-way binding naming pattern,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 279.36,
          "end": 282.84000000000003,
          "en": "and that's, therefore, the idea behind directives like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 282.84000000000003,
          "end": 285.18,
          "en": "They allow you to enhance elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 285.18,
          "end": 288.78,
          "en": "and add extra features to them, like two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 288.78,
          "end": 291.48,
          "en": "or dynamically managed CSS classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 291.48,
          "end": 293.433,
          "en": "or anything else you need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 294.75,
          "end": 299.61,
          "en": "Now, ngModel is an example for an attribute directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 299.61,
          "end": 302.61,
          "en": "Now, why is it called an attribute directive?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 302.61,
          "end": 305.55,
          "en": "Because you add it like an attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 305.55,
          "end": 307.8,
          "en": "onto an existing element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 307.8,
          "end": 312.18,
          "en": "and it then changes or enhances that element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 312.18,
          "end": 314.04,
          "en": "It may change properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 314.04,
          "end": 316.77,
          "en": "or other attributes of that element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 316.77,
          "end": 320.07,
          "en": "It may add features like two-way binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 320.07,
          "end": 322.77,
          "en": "So that's why ngModel would be an example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 322.77,
          "end": 326.7,
          "en": "for an attribute directive and we'll later also build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 326.7,
          "end": 328.953,
          "en": "a custom attribute directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 329.85,
          "end": 333.12,
          "en": "but attribute directives are not the only kind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 333.12,
          "end": 335.58,
          "en": "of directive you have in Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 335.58,
          "end": 339.423,
          "en": "instead, you also have so-called structural directives.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
